  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Scaling up EU-India Global Gateway Policy Dialogues</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The European Union is India&#xbf;s largest economic partner, with ongoing efforts to deepen ties through a comprehensive free trade agreement, which includes a Chapter on `Trade and Sustainable Development&#xbf; (TSD), and increased investment flows. Beyond economics, both sides collaborate closely on climate action, clean energy, and sustainable development, reflecting shared commitments under frameworks such as the Paris Agreement on climate change.The overall objective (impact) is to deliver on the Comprehensive Strategic Agenda endorsed at the 2026 EU&#xbf;India Summit, with a particular focus on the EU&#xbf;s Global Gateway priorities. The specific objective (outcome) is to support results- and investment-oriented policy dialogues in key areas including clean energy and climate, resilient and sustainable urbanisation, resource efficiency and circular economy, water management, education and skills, digitalisation, standardisation, and other emerging EU&#xbf;India partnership priorities.</narrative>
  </description>
